---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CaptureForm from "../../components/forms/capture-form.astro";
const seo = { page_description: "How to fill out non-interactive flat PDF forms online." };
---
<Layout title="How to Fill Non-Interactive PDF Forms" seo={seo}>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 py-16 prose">
    <h1>How to Fill Non-Interactive PDF Forms</h1>
    <p>We've all received them: a PDF form that was clearly designed to be printed and filled out by hand. There are no clickable text boxes or checkboxes (these are known as "flat" PDFs, as opposed to <a href="/reference/topic-18">AcroForms</a>).</p>

    <h2>The Digital Solution</h2>
    <p>Instead of finding a printer, you can use our <a href="/tools/add-text-to-pdf">Add Text tool</a> to type directly onto the document.</p>

    <h3>Steps to Fill the Form</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Upload:</strong> Load your flat PDF into the tool. (See our <a href="/reference/topic-2">Security Guide</a> on why doing this in the browser is safer than uploading to a server).</li>
      <li><strong>Add Text:</strong> Select the Text tool and click near the line you need to fill out.</li>
      <li><strong>Adjust:</strong> Type your answer, and drag the text box until it aligns perfectly with the printed line.</li>
      <li><strong>Sign:</strong> Use the freehand drawing tool to add your signature at the bottom.</li>
      <li><strong>Export:</strong> Save the file. The text and drawings are saved as annotations on top of the <a href="/reference/topic-17">Content Stream</a>.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Why is my text floating?</h2>
    <p>Because the PDF has no structural concept of "lines" (it's just drawing instructions), the text you add doesn't snap to the lines automatically. You must position it manually.</p>

    <div class="mt-12 not-prose p-6 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Subscribe for more workflow guides</h3>
      <CaptureForm formLabel="newsletter" submitText="Subscribe" />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
